{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1458600-spirit-combat-question-m20","id":1458600,"title":"Spirit Combat Question M20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-03T18:50:57-07:00","id":1458600,"title":"Spirit Combat Question M20","content":"Hello, I had a question about spirit combat that I somehow had overlooked. Is there a way for a mage to truly kill a spirit? (AKA: Permanently Destroy) The only thing that it says is that once a spirit is killed they simply dissapate and then reform and proceed to slumber. According to How Do You Do That? Spirit 5 + Prime 5 can damage a spirit's quintessential form making it take longer to reform, or Entropy 5 + Spirit 5 can destroy its concept, however that lasts different amounts of time depending on the spirit. So I ask you, how do you run this, and what combination of spheres do you think are required to permanently kill a spirit of average / moderate power permanently?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T19:56:19-07:00","id":1458607,"title":"","content":"In Werewolf it was always a thing to, if you want to permanently kill a spirit, drain it for Gnosis right after killing it. The current rule is short and is in W20, pp. 366.<br /> <br /> So I would rule that after reducing it to zero Essence it could be possible to destroy its Pattern permanently with those three Spheres combined, Spirit 5, Prime 5 and Entropy 5. Spirit to affect its Pattern properly, Entropy to &quot;digest&quot; and Prime to transmute the result in Quintessence.<br /> <br /> You do not quite destroy the spirit forever, but you incorporate the spirit as you would food. It is weird, but is the best I can think almost at midnight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T06:35:16-07:00","id":1458668,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on how the ST thinks of spiris and the spirit worlds. If I were the ST, I would say that a specific spirit is easy to \u201ckill\u201d, but since spirits are little more than human concepts reflected into other levels of reality, there will always be more of any particular spirit so long as the corresponding concept exists on earth. <br /> <br /> Some exceptions are unique \u201cspirits\u201d, such as physical beings that have discorprated. Such unique \u201cspirits\u201d can likewise be destroyed because they are unique - in this case they exist merely because they believe they exist, and that belief dies along with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T07:50:14-07:00","id":1458678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1458600-spirit-combat-question-m20?p=1458607#post1458607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not quite destroy the spirit forever, but you incorporate the spirit as you would food. It is weird, but is the best I can think almost at midnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've won the RAW, that's actually a canon way to do it (Well, canon for Revised. HDYDT could be taken as a retcon)<br /> <br /> In Dreamspeakers book, p. 69, there's a rote called Spirit Eating (Mind 3, Prime 3, Spirit 2): It's long, but bassically it &quot;enchants&quot; a weapon (as per Prime 2) so it can do Aggravated damage to spirits, if you damage the spirit with this weapon you eat the spirit's quintessence, and it's knowledge and memories (Mind it's for that). Also, you may get infected with mental flaws or personality traits of the spirit. &quot;Reducing a spirit\u2019s Power to zero using this spell destroys it forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Rote it's a bit too cheap for my taste, but at the same time I think HDYDT makes things more complicated than they need to be. I would allow Spirit 5/Prime 5 to do the feat (Spirit 5 to shred the spirit Essence and Gnosis, Prime 5 to annihilate it to a fundamental level). Obviously more powerful spirits are harder to deal with (practically impossible for Incarna, unless you're Voormas), and spirits can just be created again by their patrons or whatever gave birth to them in the first place (I.E: The individual it's gone, but, as they say: true evil can never be destroyed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-04-2021, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T09:30:25-07:00","id":1458683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1458600-spirit-combat-question-m20?p=1458678#post1458678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rote it's a bit too cheap for my taste, but at the same time I think HDYDT makes things more complicated than they need to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree, but was too sleepy to go deeper than RAW. Since HDYDT already states the Spheres and levels to get near to our goal, mashing all together and giving a reasonable canonical explanation is the way to go without ignoring RAW.<br /> <br /> But in this case, RAW sucks. I'm not even sure if Spirit 5 would be needed, but certainly more than 2. Several Sphere combinations could do the job in some way, and it's not as if getting there was the real challenge. To even attempt it you have to deal with the living spirit anyways, and be able to &quot;kill&quot; it somehow before attempting to KILL it for reals.<br /> <br /> The only important concept we have to take from both Dreamspeakers and Werewolf is the idea that the spirit's Gnosis/Quintessence/What-have-you must go somewhere and be incorporated into something. And it isn't even a strong mechanical or lore necessity, is just a theme, as long as killing a spirit permanently requires a bit more effort and quick action than just beating it, everything's fine.<br /> <br /> What about Spirit 4, Prime 4 and at least 2 in the Sphere of the thing you're going to shove that Quintessence? Spirit 4 is enough to Bind, and other spheres/actions are doing the Pattern unraveling. Prime 4 lets you drain Quintessence from non-living targets and also imbue it into targets to create permanent Wonders. Since you are already using Spirit and spirits aren't precisely living things, I would deem it enough after the spirit is properly beaten down. With 2 in Matter, Mind or Life you have the ability to make the first basic alterations to such Patterns, enough to imbue them with the Quintessence without changing them dramatically. But also without protecting them from unpredicted consequences.<br /> <br /> Optionally, if I was feeling particularly forgiving, I would even stretch things a little to let this be done with Spirit 3, Prime 3, Entropy 3 and Matter/Life/Mind 3. But then isn't something I recommend unless the ST thinks access to this option s is more important to the chronicle than being strict with normal Spheres limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}